{
  "dom_id": "step-q94701",
  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Find the $30$th percentile of the random variable $Y$ if the probability distribution function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y},\\, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $Y$ is the number ${y}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le {y}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $30$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.3.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le {y}_{0.3}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{{y}_{0.3}}{e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{e}^{-y}{|}_{0}^{{y}_{0.3}} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-{y}_{0.3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $30$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-{y}_{0.3}} & =0.3 \\\\ {e}^{-{y}_{0.3}} & =0.7 \\\\ {e}^{-{y}_{0.3}} & =\\frac{7}{10} \\\\ -{y}_{0.3} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{10}) \\\\ {y}_{0.3} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{10}{7}) \\\\ {y}_{0.3} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
